## 4. Explicit follow-ups from the report

These ideas are retained but not hidden inside the increments above:

| Idea | Disposition and reason |
|---|---|
| `fit_arc` / bounded arc sampling | Follow-up after native arcs. Needs a clear point-range/handle editing contract and a distinction between inscribed chords and tangent-safe exterior fitting. A sagitta bound alone does not guarantee clearance from an inner wall. |
| `clip_outside` | Deferred geometry feature: boolean ownership, live dependency and mesh/query parity need their own design. Explicit hole targets do not implement clipping solids against rooms. |
| General `measure_geometry` | Deferred until concrete remaining query gaps are identified; reuse existing path/surface tools where possible. No arbitrary expression evaluator. |
| Cross-group room-interior intrusion lint | Deferred diagnostic prototype. Intentional intersecting floors, galleries and door surrounds make bounding-box overlap insufficient. Requires geometry-aware depth/clearance, tolerances, exclusions and a measured false-positive fixture. Do not promise exact distances from coarse bounds. |
| Cut groups | Address the immediate problem through explicit target lists and inspection first; revisit named reusable cut sets only if target-list authoring proves insufficient. |
| Terrain-aware Walk/placement/queries | Remains phase 16 §10 follow-up, not silently included here. |

## 5. Delivery and verification

Order: 19.1 → 19.2 → 19.3 → 19.4 → 19.5 → 19.6 → 19.7 → 19.8. The editor and geometry increments can ship independently; integration fixtures accumulate as features land. Geometry contract questions are resolved in the owning increment before production changes, with decisions written below.

For every implementation increment:

- Read applicable prior plan requirements and record decisions, relevant files, checks, limitations and next steps in Progress. Add implemented terms to `GLOSSARY.md`; proposed fields here are not yet glossary contracts.
- Run focused behavioral regressions, `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build:web`. Use real MCP requests for schema/error/atomicity changes and browser checks for interactions. Bump the MCP patch version when its public contract changes.
- Use `PORT=5171 DATA_DIR=<scratch>/data npm run dev` or another free port with a separate scratch folder. Create/read scene fixtures through MCP or the editor only. Never inspect or edit project data files directly.
- Check one-command undo, failed-call atomicity, old scene defaults, save/reload, dependencies and copied references for persisted changes. Verify captures use canonical geometry and selection overlays do not leak into exports.
- Geometry/orientation changes require GLB and real scratch Unity import/collider checks even if importer code is unchanged. Compile importer changes with `scripts/compile-unity.sh` where available; compilation alone is not visual acceptance. Preserve Unity Claim/drift and phase 18 node ownership.
- Keep performance checks proportional: large nested scene for hover/reveal; bounded results for reads; item limits for arrays; affected-target invalidation for cuts/attachments. Do not introduce scene-wide pointer work or unrelated renderer optimization.

